, "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 383329, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HVhyi3jc4NqGnWBNaAHDpK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 389027, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That made `test_half_even` fail: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 in the advisory system, but it isn't listed there, so the expected behaviour comes from the test and the docstring. I didn't merge the PR because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015wv3eXtsLJ5ZjgrWwPd4zD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LArfXiM9CUHx7but16hhX4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019tud6szGGm42t2cYRLPHz4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CHtPgknsjdb5rpPSzJ7d5M"